Files, copied byte for byte from the WDGoNG 0.10.0 source archive:

    adsb_tracks.py     from  wdgong_ui/adsb_tracks.py
                       ADS-B track loading, receiver coverage, KML export.
    subghz_export.py   from  watchdogs/subghz_export.py
                       rtl_433 raw I/Q (.cu8) -> Flipper Zero RAW .sub.
    basemap.py         from  watchdogs/basemap.py
                       MBTiles reader + tile maths for the offline world map.

    SHA-256 (first 16 hex digits), identical to the source archive:
        72A497587444217D  adsb_tracks.py
        CFC0A6526ACB3D84  subghz_export.py
        B4DEF0C6C6D3676F  basemap.py
        072C5C8D537A1E49  LICENSE-WDGoNG.txt  (WDGoNG's LICENSE)

    NOT included: WDGoNG's map data file, wdgong_ui/assets/map/basemap.mbtiles
    (about 29 MB). It is not part of the WDGoNG 0.10.0 source archive. The
    plugin uses it when the player copies it in (see plugins/ng_basemap.py).

They are not modified. The code that connects them to upstream edition's pyxel game
is in plugins/ng_adsb_tracks.py and plugins/ng_subghz_capture.py; those two
plugins were written for this build and follow the behaviour of WDGoNG's
backend (wdgong_ui/backend.py: _adsb_rx_log, adsb_tracks, adsb_export_kml;
watchdogs/sdr_manager.py: start_433_grab, _grab_watcher), so they are covered
by the same licence terms and notice.

Two more WDGoNG features have no separate source file to copy (they live
inside wdgong_ui/backend.py) and were written again for this build after
WDGoNG's behaviour; they carry the same notice and licence terms:

    plugins/ng_loot_backup.py, plugins/_loot_backup.py
                       loot backup / restore to one file
                       (backend.py: export_userdata, import_userdata)
    plugins/kismet_wardrive.py: _ensure_gps
                       GPS switched on automatically when a wardrive starts
                       (backend.py: ensure_gps)
    plugins/ng_wdgwars.py
                       WDGWars pairing by code and the rank / team / territory
                       status (backend.py: pair_start, _pair_worker,
                       _fetch_gs_worker; main.py's game-state overlays). No
                       portal code of WDGoNG's is used: every request goes
                       through upstream's own Wars Sync client.
    plugins/ng_basemap.py
                       draws the offline world map from basemap.py's tiles in
                       pyxel (main.py's basemap drawing, re-done for 16 colours)
    plugins/ng_433_hunter.py
                       433 MHz fox hunt with the RTL-SDR: WDGoNG's detection
                       maths and KEY_HUNT_* constants (watchdogs/sdr_manager.py:
                       start_key_hunt, _key_hunt_reader, keyhunt_learn)
    plugins/ng_session_log.py
                       loot session journal: browse sessions, preview files
                       (main.py's loot screen SESSION LOG)
    plugins/_loot_backup.py: auto_copy_db, damaged_db_hint
                       rolling known-good copy of loot_db.json while playing
                       (README "periodic auto-backup of the loot DB")

One defect of a copied file is corrected OUTSIDE that file, so the copy stays
byte-identical: subghz_export.cu8_to_pulses() can emit two timings of the same
sign in a row on a noisy recording, which is not valid Flipper RAW data.
plugins/ng_subghz_capture.py: repair_raw_sub() joins such neighbours after
the .sub has been written.

plugins/ng_subghz_capture.py also differs from WDGoNG's _grab_watcher on
purpose: every capture gets a folder of its own, a .sub is written only from a
recording that is complete and not empty (also after Stop), and the .sub is
renamed into place when it is complete. The copied converter is unchanged.

One WDGoNG bug fix is ported into upstream's own code rather than kept here:
watchdogs/loot_manager.py counts a session's ADS-B aircraft as distinct ICAO
codes (WDGoNG watchdogs/loot_manager.py: _fix_adsb_counts and the session
scan). It is tagged [merge-v3] in that file.

